  data: {
    LLM: '1. **Turn**: Play one card face-up, place a chip on the matching unoccupied board space (or use jack power). 2. **Draw**: Replenish hand from stock. 3. **Two-eyed jack** (clubs, diamonds): Wildâ€”place your chip on any unoccupied space. 4. **One-eyed jack** (hearts, spades): Remove one opponent chip from the board. 5. **Win**: First player/team to complete a row of five chips wins.',
    Player: "Play a card, put a chip on the matching space. Two-eyed jacks let you place on any empty space. One-eyed jacks let you remove an opponent's chip. First to get five in a row wins.",
    objective: "Form one or more rows of five chips of your colour (or your team's) on the board. Rows can be horizontal, vertical, or diagonal.",
    gameplay: '1. **Turn**: Play one card face-up, place a chip on the matching unoccupied board space (or use jack power). 2. **Draw**: Replenish hand from stock. 3. **Two-eyed jack** (clubs, diamonds): Wildâ€”place your chip on any unoccupied space. 4. **One-eyed jack** (hearts, spades): Remove one opponent chip from the board. 5. **Win**: First player/team to complete a row of five chips wins.',
